A||||2||PatrickB||Some good advice||||3||
Z||000000||PatrickB||01-31-2001||10:35 AM||||Unfortunately a lot of good advice comes in learning from a mistake and this is one of those...<P>About a week ago in my sister's boyfriend's garage there was an accident that killed his neighbor.  The neighbor and my sister's boyfriend share a garage that is seperated from the house by about 20 feet.  It was really cold and they had some big lake effect snow so the neighbor took out his snowblower to clean up.  He was getting everything ready inside the garage and was fueling it up apparently with the doors closed.  He left for about 10-15 minutes and came back inside the garage and flicked the light switch.<BR>When he turned on the switch it ingited the gasoline vapors blowing up the whole garage and killing himself.  The flames were so hot it melted the siding on the side of the house.<P>It seems like one of those things that you see in the movies and Im sure its something that many of us have done or something similar and never realized.  Just from filling up a lawnmower or snowblower or anything is enough.  Especially in the winter time when its cold outside and you keep your garage doors closed.<P>So next time your working on the fiero, filling something up with gasoline, or working with any flammables remember to have really good ventilation.||||reg||3
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-31-2001||10:58 AM||||Im sorry to hear that.  I have heard stories from people at work that once had to go to a house where natural gas was leaking.  They always tell people, do NOT touch anything, even static electricity arcing will blow your house up.  Sometimes people take turning on lights for granted, and the person with the house did and blew himself out the front window into the street, luckily he survived.<P>My condolences to the family of the neighbor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||01-31-2001||01:59 PM||||My GF's grandfather owned a service station and was pumping gas from a car into a gas can and something sparked and blew the place up. The doors blew right off. He was burned over 30% and almost died. I think it happened like 15 years ago. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
